# Text files are checked out exactly as they are stored, on every machine. Without this, Git for Windows' default
# (core.autocrlf=true) rewrites LF files to CRLF at checkout, which breaks the bash scripts under
# tools/porting/livetest. Files already stored with CRLF stay as they are (nothing is renormalized).
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.zip binary
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
*.asi binary
*.bin binary
*.dmp binary
